{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1100543-dropping-instruments-wise-what-constitutes-a-technomancer","id":1100543,"title":"Dropping Instruments-wise, what constitutes a Technomancer?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-06-05T13:01:06-07:00","id":1100543,"title":"Dropping Instruments-wise, what constitutes a Technomancer?","content":"First and foremost, we already know that some people on this forum disagree with how M20 does the process of overcoming Instruments. There's an entire other thread discussing it. For that very reason, let's avoid tracking that subject in here, and assume M20 RAW. That Mystics start overcoming Instruments at Arete 3, Technomancers start overcoming at Arete 6, and Technocrats keep their Instruments until Arete 10. With me so far?<br /> <br /> Okay, except I've been thinking about the division between Mystic and Technomancer. And, more specifically, about which groups belong to which category. Where the dividing line is.<br /> <br /> Obviously, Traditions like the Virtual Adepts and Society of Ether undoubtedly fall into the Technomancer camp, even when some of their number dabble in occult science (for, indeed, sufficiently analyzed magic is indistinguishable from Science). These are uncontroversial placements.<br /> <br /> But what about factions within otherwise Mystic Traditions and Crafts, who don't just dabble in science and tech, but use them heavily? At what point does a mage cease to be a Mystic whose tools include tech, and become a Technomancer with a Mystic's worldview? I suppose a better question would be at what point a mage becomes so dependent on their tools, they cease being able to readily see their magick as separate from them?<br /> <br /> If we assume the latter is more important, then certain groups that are nominally Mystic might be better run as Technomancers. The Children of Knowledge are a big example, as their Alchemy is just as much Science as it is Art. As far back as the Book of Crafts, they were stated to have many of the advantages of a Technomancer - tools that blend into the Consensus more readily - and were not allowed to overcome their Foci. Obviously, M20 is more charitable in this regard, but the logic is still sound. So it's fully reasonable to expect Solificati to not be able to overcome Instruments until Arete 6+.<br /> <br /> A slightly different example that raises questions is Hermetic House Verditus. The parts of that House that were holdovers from House Thig are much more obviously technomancer. But it's the &quot;Classic&quot; Verditus magi that interest me here. Their tools are more ancient and their worldview very Hermetic, but they still use those tools extensively. Going back to MtAs's spiritual predecessor, Ars Magica, House Verditus were Gifted individuals who had a House-wide Flaw: a dependency on ritual tools, when their fellow Hermetic magi could get away with just verbal and somatic components. While the Order of Hermes in Ars Magica is not the same Order of Hermes in Mage: The Ascension, they are parallel Orders with parallel ethos. It stands to reason, then, that a craft wizard might be so dependent on their creations, they would count as Technomancers for the purposes of overcoming Instruments.<br /> <br /> As with all things in the World of Darkness, how this whole matter works out is dependent on the Storyteller.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T15:04:12-07:00","id":1100601,"title":"","content":"I believe the intent was to give some &quot;balance&quot; to the easier Coincidence for Technomancers vs Mystics. Along with giving both supreme advantages over Technocrats. That being said Modern Verditus are Technomancers. They readily incorporate technology into their craft. They were always using the best techiques available for their craft they are just the most willing to steal back from the Technocracy.<br /> <br /> So I personally would generally treat a Verditus as a Technomancer and probably would give them Order of Reason levels in Sorcerer Crusade(Same with Solfacti)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T15:12:51-07:00","id":1100610,"title":"","content":"I think it depends on what the Storyteller believes is the source of the mage's increased dependence on the tool.<br /> <br /> I tend to see the tool dependence as less dependent on whether or not something is Science vs. Art (I think most of the Hermetics would arguably fall on the former, by the same logic that the Alchemists do. Even the most Mystickal Hermetic uses geometry, formulas, and tried and true, for them, methodology) and more as a reflection of what society believes is possible right now.<br /> <br /> Basically, the average person might look at most of the bog standard Etherite or Virtual Adept tricks and think &quot;oh yeah, that's possible&quot;, and not think too much about it. It gives them an advantage when it comes to vulgar vs. coincidental, but a disadvantage, I think, because the Mage arguably is still relying on that faint glimmer of possibility like a crutch. Somewhere in the back of their mind, a low arete Scientist may still be thinking &quot;yeah, but this is ACTUALLY possible. Not like those wand wavers.&quot;<br /> <br /> In contrast, the Solificati might be using a tried and true method to turn lead into gold, but almost no one in modern society actually believes that's possible. So assuming the Solificati has a modern American upbringing, she's got a head start in realizing &quot;Oh, crap, I am really doing the impossible.&quot; And I think that once you make that mental leap, it becomes easier to realize that a lot of your limitations are self-imposed. And therefore, you can shed them.<br /> <br /> The Etherite WILL come to that conclusion eventually too, but in a society that grew up on sci-fi movies, it's going to take a little longer for him to realize exactly how impossible his work is. And until he does, he will reinforce his mistaken belief that his tools are necessary.<br /> <br /> I think, for Thig/Vertidus technomancers, I wouldn't use the technomancer limitation. Because even granted that they are technomancers, they're still being trained and educated in the overall Order of Hermes. They're still going to have the foundation in the more impossible arts, even if their own methods are a bit closer to home.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2430,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","user":"kalinara","date":".  freudian typos are annoying 06-05-2017, 07:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T16:10:50-07:00","id":1100629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kalinara</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1100543-dropping-instruments-wise-what-constitutes-a-technomancer?p=1100610#post1100610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In contrast, the Solificati might be using a tried and true method to turn lead into gold, but almost no one in modern society actually believes that's possible. So assuming the Solificati has a modern American upbringing, she's got a head start in realizing &quot;Oh, crap, I am really doing the impossible.&quot; And I think that once you make that mental leap, it becomes easier to realize that a lot of your limitations are self-imposed. And therefore, you can shed them.</div> </div> </div> </div>The reasoning stated in Book of Crafts for why Solificati can't overcome Instruments is that, regardless of the deeply symbolic and mythical underpinnings of the art, Alchemy LOOKS a whole lot like Chemistry. If someone takes a vial from a pocket, pours its contents on a concrete wall, and a section of the wall dissolves, most people would assume that it's some kind of strong acid. It doesn't matter that the character is using a fluid derived from crocodile bladders and Nile river sand, and used it to perform a Matter 3 Effect. If a Hermetic, meanwhile, pointed a wand at the wall and uttered a phrase in Latin, and obtained the same effect, that would be obvious mysticism.<br /> <br /> Same thing if the Crowned One caused someone to hallucinate by spiking their drink, or made their shoes quieter by applying some weird powder, or caused someone to become ill by hitting them with a smoke grenade. Those Instruments were all created using Alchemical principles, yet they conform to Consensus expectations more readily than the Hermetic's showy wizardry. It's the adage &quot;Better Living Through Chemistry&quot; put to practice, and modern people trust Chemistry as a Science.<br /> <br /> That's the reasoning from the book, anyway. The Solificato believes they are doing Science (or, rather, Natural Philosophy), and that it's their use of the right materials in the right proportions that makes the magick happen. Their tools serve them well in today's ideological climate...but that also makes them more likely to lean on them as a CRUTCH (not crux). They are dependent on outside resources for their magick, making it all the harder to let them go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T16:18:41-07:00","id":1100635,"title":"","content":"I admit, it's been a long time since I've read the Book of Crafts. Thank you for the reference!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2430,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","user":"kalinara","date":". 06-05-2017, 08:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-06T09:57:44-07:00","id":1100869,"title":"","content":"I have made which of the three paths are taken a player choice for their characters along the lines of picking Practice, Paradigm and Instruments. And it doesn't always track with the Technocrat, technomancer, mystic attribution of the various groups.<br /> <br /> For example, there are NWO agents who really get close to being mystics. If their Instruments are things like kinesics, proximics, memetics, then it's fairly easy to see one of them gradually dropping the various particular Instruments and getting closer and closer to something like psychic. &quot;How did he get that guy to do that?&quot; &quot;I dunno. His subliminalization of his active memetics is phenomenal!&quot;<br /> <br /> And there are Hermetics (as per the Solificati above) who will NEVER give up their toys, such as a lot of the dudes in House Verditus.<br /> <br /> Oh, and it is possible to change your path if that's the way your Focus evolves as Arete goes up. I have a menu of choices that can be made when that happens which builds out from the standard &quot;mystics surpass one Instrument&quot; to allow for adding more Instruments, making them work as if you surpassed them in that they reduce difficulty but you still need them to create effects, allowing for a specific personal Instrument to be named while still keeping the more generalized Instrument as a whole in play, and so on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1062,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","user":"Ajax","date":". 06-06-2017, 07:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-07T07:23:47-07:00","id":1101210,"title":"","content":"My go to distinction for the difference between Mystics and Technomancers is whether they internalize or externalize their magic. Or to put it another way, do they separate themselves from their magic or not?<br /> <br /> Those who consider the Mage to be an intrinsic part of the magic fall on the Mystic side. This includes the Akashics who consider their forms and meditations to be a guide to real enlightenment, the Choristers who consider themselves to be one part of the conversation with the divine, and the Chakravanti who consider their proper place within the wheel to be what guides them. Even most Hermetics fall on this side because they consider an Enlightened Will to be a vital component of their otherwise highly formalized magic.<br /> <br /> Those who think magic is a mostly independent matter of cause and effect are Technomancers. The mage may be special for being able to see and understand how and why these things work, but she doesn't make them work. By happenstance most of the mages who fall into this category are Etherites and VAs, since technology tends to be external by default. Some few Hermetics might as well, as would many members of Sorcerous groups who awakened to True Magic.<br /> <br /> Separate a Technomancer from his tools and you deprive the mage of his magic. Separate a Mystic from his tools and you deprive his tools of theirs.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-08T02:42:57-07:00","id":1101544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1100543-dropping-instruments-wise-what-constitutes-a-technomancer?p=1100869#post1100869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For example, there are NWO agents who really get close to being mystics. If their Instruments are things like kinesics, proximics, memetics, then it's fairly easy to see one of them gradually dropping the various particular Instruments and getting closer and closer to something like psychic. &quot;How did he get that guy to do that?&quot; &quot;I dunno. His subliminalization of his active memetics is phenomenal!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>The way I understand how Technocrats work, is that they can't actually do this. There is only so much an NWO member can do in a single, isolated interaction, if they have no favorable context, aren't dressed for effect, haven't analyzed the person...they simply can't do anything special other than perhaps make a slightly positive impression. Just as a Progenitor can't modify DNA without their Foci, so also there is no dropping Instruments for Technocrats, when it comes to the social/humanistic Procedures and Adjustments. Of course an Arete 5+ NWO member might get really good at reading subtle cues, and smiling, shaking hand etc. in the right way...but there is only so much this can do - 99 % of the time it certainly won't make the waiter at the restaurant skip the payment part of the dinner; it must be Coincidental, unlike the Mind capabilities of the more mystically inclined Mages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 06-08-2017, 05:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-08T09:14:05-07:00","id":1101657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1100543-dropping-instruments-wise-what-constitutes-a-technomancer?p=1101544#post1101544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The way I understand how Technocrats work, is that they can't actually do this. There is only so much an NWO member can do in a single, isolated interaction, if they have no favorable context, aren't dressed for effect, haven't analyzed the person...they simply can't do anything special other than perhaps make a slightly positive impression. Just as a Progenitor can't modify DNA without their Foci, so also there is no dropping Instruments for Technocrats, when it comes to the social/humanistic Procedures and Adjustments. Of course an Arete 5+ NWO member might get really good at reading subtle cues, and smiling, shaking hand etc. in the right way...but there is only so much this can do - 99 % of the time it certainly won't make the waiter at the restaurant skip the payment part of the dinner; it must be Coincidental, unlike the Mind capabilities of the more mystically inclined Mages.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I don't think it needs to be coincidental. Modern Technocrats, unlike their Order of Reason predecessors, aren't beholden to a &quot;Casual Rule&quot;. They can still do activities Vulgar by the standards of the Consensus. What really constrains them is whether they have an Instrument at all.<br /> <br /> Which is the problem inherent to Technocrats. They aren't just technomancers, they're people who have undergone Conditioning, such that it categorically excludes even the <i>idea</i> of using Enlightened Science without tools. Their programming won't allow it. So it doesn't matter how Enlightened they become, they are dependent on their tools in ways not even Virtual Adepts or Etherites are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-08T13:12:34-07:00","id":1101713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1100543-dropping-instruments-wise-what-constitutes-a-technomancer?p=1101657#post1101657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I don't think it needs to be coincidental. Modern Technocrats, unlike their Order of Reason predecessors, aren't beholden to a &quot;Casual Rule&quot;. They can still do activities Vulgar by the standards of the Consensus. What really constrains them is whether they have an Instrument at all.<br /> <br /> Which is the problem inherent to Technocrats. They aren't just technomancers, they're people who have undergone Conditioning, such that it categorically excludes even the <i>idea</i> of using Enlightened Science without tools. Their programming won't allow it. So it doesn't matter how Enlightened they become, they are dependent on their tools in ways not even Virtual Adepts or Etherites are.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you are hacking the web with your mind by just standing there and thinking about it, are you still a VA? If you are hacking reality and making apples out of nothing, are you still a VA? <br /> <br /> If you are disintigrating things with a disinitigration ray with no disintigration ray gun, just thinking about forming a disintigration ray, are you still an Etherite?<br /> <br /> If a MiB can just stand there and intimidate you by doing absolutely nothing, just &quot;being intimidating&quot; is he still a member of the NWO?<br /> <br /> This is why I agree with part of the point Dataweaver made in another thread (I think). The Purple Paradigm is actually more of a failing to Mage than it is a benefit. The absolute WORST Mage players I have ever had the misfortune to play with are the ones who have their mage's &quot;just do things&quot; without any recourse to even the hints of Focus that existed before M20 (e.g. &quot;paradigm&quot;). And, apparently, that kind of play is the GOAL of the game under the Purple Paradigm. Mages who just stand there and magic happens around them because they will it so. All the player needs to do is say &quot;My mage uses Matter 2 and makes bread fall from the sky. and then uses Forces 2 to toast it before it hits the ground&quot;. No need to say HOW the mage does so. No Pratice needed. No Instruments. <br /> <br /> Boring. (Unless it's a Marauder, in which case all sorts of other interesting things are probably happening). Give me Foci all the way up to Arete 10. Not that they can't change as the mage's understanding of magic evolves, but not that they vanish and leave them as either children saying &quot;Because I WANNA have it that way&quot; or really bad role-players who say &quot;I use Matter 2 to do X and don't ask &quot;How?&quot; I do it because the rules say I can!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-08T13:41:48-07:00","id":1101720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1100543-dropping-instruments-wise-what-constitutes-a-technomancer?p=1101713#post1101713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you are hacking the web with your mind by just standing there and thinking about it, are you still a VA? If you are hacking reality and making apples out of nothing, are you still a VA?<br /> <br /> If you are disintigrating things with a disinitigration ray with no disintigration ray gun, just thinking about forming a disintigration ray, are you still an Etherite?<br /> <br /> If a MiB can just stand there and intimidate you by doing absolutely nothing, just &quot;being intimidating&quot; is he still a member of the NWO?<br /> <br /> This is why I agree with part of the point Dataweaver made in another thread (I think). The Purple Paradigm is actually more of a failing to Mage than it is a benefit. The absolute WORST Mage players I have ever had the misfortune to play with are the ones who have their mage's &quot;just do things&quot; without any recourse to even the hints of Focus that existed before M20 (e.g. &quot;paradigm&quot;). And, apparently, that kind of play is the GOAL of the game under the Purple Paradigm. Mages who just stand there and magic happens around them because they will it so. All the player needs to do is say &quot;My mage uses Matter 2 and makes bread fall from the sky. and then uses Forces 2 to toast it before it hits the ground&quot;. No need to say HOW the mage does so. No Pratice needed. No Instruments.<br /> <br /> Boring. (Unless it's a Marauder, in which case all sorts of other interesting things are probably happening). Give me Foci all the way up to Arete 10. Not that they can't change as the mage's understanding of magic evolves, but not that they vanish and leave them as either children saying &quot;Because I WANNA have it that way&quot; or really bad role-players who say &quot;I use Matter 2 to do X and don't ask &quot;How?&quot; I do it because the rules say I can!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>All true. Having the characters be able to just discard their Instruments entirely can be boring.<br /> <br /> But if they never use their Instruments again, they also never get the -1 difficulty for using an Instrument when they don't need it. So there's still an incentive to roleplay one's Focus. With the more powerful Sphere Effects, every reduction in difficulty can be vital. Moreso if the character is under adverse conditions and is low on Quintessence.<br /> <br /> There's also the fact that certain Paradigms - technomancers especially - would also benefit from their Instruments if they made them more coincidental. Hacking the web with a computer is more believable than just thinking about it. As is intimidating someone by glaring and making harsh eye contact (while wearing an outfit like a government spook). Disintegrating things is usually Vulgar no matter if it's done with a ray gun or not, but chucking a huge bottle of &quot;acid&quot; is coincidental.<br /> <br /> I can think of one other way a Storyteller could induce the players to be more creative with their magic: Experience points. The Storyteller is free to reward good roleplaying with more XP points. It could be decided that the players need to make their use of magic interesting, or they'll lose out on points (which are always in shorter supply than any player would like, but even shorter at high levels where everything is expensive).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-08T17:32:26-07:00","id":1101808,"title":"","content":"I've been a fan of consolation on technomancer tools, you start out with a utility belt worth of stuff and end up with a Swiss army knife/sonic screwdriver of sorts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T01:16:49-07:00","id":1101885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1100543-dropping-instruments-wise-what-constitutes-a-technomancer?p=1101657#post1101657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I don't think it needs to be coincidental. Modern Technocrats, unlike their Order of Reason predecessors, aren't beholden to a &quot;Casual Rule&quot;. They can still do activities Vulgar by the standards of the Consensus. What really constrains them is whether they have an Instrument at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>I meant the NWO. The NWO's psychology-and-talking based expertise has no Vulgar options. If an NWO got someone to do something through interaction, then it's Coincidental, as far as I see it - even if the average person would claim &quot;No way he convinced him of this!&quot;.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1100543-dropping-instruments-wise-what-constitutes-a-technomancer?p=1101657#post1101657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which is the problem inherent to Technocrats. They aren't just technomancers, they're people who have undergone Conditioning, such that it categorically excludes even the <i>idea</i> of using Enlightened Science without tools. Their programming won't allow it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's also more than Conditioning - some Technocrats see it as a personal, long-term choice of developing their potential in such a way. If this means that they can't do anything without their Instruments, then this is something that they accept. Especially, I think, those of the Pattern Essence.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1100543-dropping-instruments-wise-what-constitutes-a-technomancer?p=1101657#post1101657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> If a MiB can just stand there and intimidate you by doing absolutely nothing, just &quot;being intimidating&quot; is he still a member of the NWO?</div> </div> </div> </div>While some descriptions of Technocrat Procedures and Adjustments make it seem like this is possible, I'd say that such True Magick can only be done primarily by the Ecstatics and the Hollow Ones - and even by them, only under select circumstances.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1100543-dropping-instruments-wise-what-constitutes-a-technomancer?p=1101713#post1101713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you are disintigrating things with a disinitigration ray with no disintigration ray gun, just thinking about forming a disintigration ray, are you still an Etherite?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is an interesting question. In the recent thread about abandoning Foci Dataweaver suggested the idea of Foci dealing with Paradox; assuming this, you could have the radical senior Etherites who indeed use 'do-the-equations-in-the-head' for their Effects...while on the other (or should it be: 'another' ?) side you have the play-it-safe Etherites who will always insist on doing things properly with machines and devices.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 06-09-2017, 02:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T05:42:04-07:00","id":1101942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1100543-dropping-instruments-wise-what-constitutes-a-technomancer?p=1101713#post1101713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you are hacking the web with your mind by just standing there and thinking about it, are you still a VA? If you are hacking reality and making apples out of nothing, are you still a VA?<br /> <br /> If you are disintigrating things with a disinitigration ray with no disintigration ray gun, just thinking about forming a disintigration ray, are you still an Etherite?<br /> <br /> If a MiB can just stand there and intimidate you by doing absolutely nothing, just &quot;being intimidating&quot; is he still a member of the NWO?</div> </div> </div> </div>That depends on what the mage is thinking about, doesn't it? A VA with a 'hacking the source code of the Universe' paradigm may eventually realize that since his mind is already connected with the Universe he can use that direct connection rather than his complicated computer setup. Sure, he's standing there and thinking about it, but he's still hacking the source code of the universe. He dropped his tools, not his practice.<br /> <br /> Likewise the Etherite might realize that the strange forces he was building machines to manipulate are so interconnected that it is nearly always possible to trigger an effect similar to what he's looking for with a few carefully considered movements. Or a creative application of the Copenhagen Interpretation to collapse the waveforms just so. Or manipulating his internal etheric energies to set the right vibrations in motion. The possibilities for dropping tools while keeping practice are endless.<br /> <br /> And the MiB Agent can focus really hard on the Jungian principles that represent humans fear. And then he can go cry in a corner because Technocrats don't get to do that. Why oh why did he leave the office without his regulation black suit and mirrorshades, anyways?<br /> <br /> The Purple Paradigm problem (this part, anyways) has more do with people assuming that tools are the same thing as paradigm/practice. There's no reason to assume that, and indeed with the Mystical factions we often don't. Yoda stopped needing to meditate, but no one would ever say he stopped using the Force. No one thinks Dumbledore stopped using magic just because he didn't always make some incantation. There are considerably fewer examples of scientists realizing they didn't need lab equipment because the real understanding was in them all along, but that doesn't mean they don't do the same thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":758,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","user":"Ramnesis","date":". 06-09-2017, 11:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T08:35:02-07:00","id":1101995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1100543-dropping-instruments-wise-what-constitutes-a-technomancer?p=1101942#post1101942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That depends on what the mage is thinking about, doesn't it? A VA with a 'hacking the source code of the Universe' paradigm may eventually realize that since his mind is already connected with the Universe and he can use that direct connection rather than his complicated computer setup. Sure, he's standing there and thinking about it, but he's still hacking the source code of the universe. He dropped his tools, not his practice.<br /> <br /> Likewise the Etherite might realize that the strange forces he was building machines to manipulate are so interconnected that it is nearly always possible to trigger an effect similar to what he's looking for with a few carefully considered movements. Or a creative application of the Copenhagen Interpretation to collapse the waveforms just so. Or manipulating his internal etheric energies to set the right vibrations in motion. The possibilities for dropping tools while keeping practice are endless.<br /> <br /> And the MiB Agent can focus really hard on the Jungian principles that represent humans fear. And then he can go cry in a corner because Technocrats don't get to do that. Why oh why did he leave the office without his regulation black suit and mirrorshades, anyways?<br /> <br /> The Purple Paradigm problem (this part, anyways) has more do with people assuming that tools are the same thing as paradigm/practice. There's no reason to assume that, and indeed with the Mystical factions we often don't. Yoda stopped needing to meditate, but no one would ever say he stopped using the Force. No one thinks Dumbledore stopped using magic just because he didn't always make some incantation. There are considerably fewer examples of scientists realizing they didn't need lab equipment because the real understanding was in them all along, but that doesn't mean they don't do the same thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>This, exactly.<br /> <br /> It's why I like how M20 explained Focus better than how previous editions explained Paradigm and Foci. With Focus, the three elements - Paradigm, Practice, and Instruments - are given equal importance to how a mage does magic, and how they believe they do magic. It creates a, for lack of better word, Paradigm Shift in how players think about the subject. In this case, a mage's magic isn't just the tools they use, but the methodology behind those tools, and ultimately the worldview that makes that methodology possible in the first place. Even when a mage gets Enlightened enough to surpass their Instruments, that doesn't necessarily mean they've abandoned their Paradigm and Practice.<br /> <br /> I've maintained before that characters with Arete 6+ are not required to reject their Paradigms to explain why they don't need the Instruments of their Practice. They come up with reasonable explanations for their increased mastery, based entirely within those Paradigms. A Hermetic master believes he's honed his True Will to an edge sharp enough to cut Reality into any shape he desires. A Chorister sees their mastery as a relationship with the One that is so solid, they need not make open and involved requests, because their very life is an active prayer. Even technomancers can do this with the right rationalization. The Virtual Adept understands the hacking process well enough that their minds do the work their computer systems once did. A Solificati arch master has truly become a Crowned One, her spirit having been transmuted to True Gold, and can alone act as a catalyst for changing the world around them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T11:31:00-07:00","id":1102051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1100543-dropping-instruments-wise-what-constitutes-a-technomancer?p=1101995#post1101995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've maintained before that characters with Arete 6+ are not required to reject their Paradigms to explain why they don't need the Instruments of their Practice. They come up with reasonable explanations for their increased mastery, based entirely within those Paradigms.</div> </div> </div> </div>A high Arete Cultist of Ecstasy has already experienced so much - and weaved Magick through her or his life and the life through Magick - that they can call upon True Magick without necessarily experiencing those things. They have lived through them, and what they went through will always be within an Ecstatic. (Or something along these lines.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 06-09-2017, 02:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T18:34:09-07:00","id":1102168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1100543-dropping-instruments-wise-what-constitutes-a-technomancer?p=1101942#post1101942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Purple Paradigm problem (this part, anyways) has more do with people assuming that tools are the same thing as paradigm/practice. There's no reason to assume that, and indeed with the Mystical factions we often don't. Yoda stopped needing to meditate, but no one would ever say he stopped using the Force. No one thinks Dumbledore stopped using magic just because he didn't always make some incantation. There are considerably fewer examples of scientists realizing they didn't need lab equipment because the real understanding was in them all along, but that doesn't mean they don't do the same thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, with the advent of Focus, THEY ARE. If Instruments just included magic words, circle, gadgets, whatever, you might might be right, but with ideas and thoughts being Instruments and Instruments existing within the framework of Practice.... It's not a vague-ish &quot;thing&quot; out there like pre-M20 paradigm was. If Tools = Instruments then they do link so tight into paradigm/practice that there is no space in between any longer. And that is what makes the Purple Paradigm slightly wonky now... Because if Practice and Instruments can equate to thoughts and intentions and gestures, then the Purple Paradigm is saying that even THOSE are being given up. So not only does magic become flavorless pap where something just happens (something indescribable for vulgar or something that could make sense if not), but it's actually going to happen in an indescribable way. With no thought or intention or action.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1062,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","user":"Ajax","date":". 06-10-2017, 10:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-10T01:39:43-07:00","id":1102217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1100543-dropping-instruments-wise-what-constitutes-a-technomancer?p=1102168#post1102168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually, with the advent of Focus, THEY ARE. If Instruments just included magic words, circle, gadgets, whatever, you might might be right, but with ideas and thoughts being Instruments and Instruments existing within the framework of Practice.... It's not a vague-ish &amp;quot;thing&amp;quot; out there like pre-M20 paradigm was. If Tools = Instruments then they do link so tight into paradigm/practice that there is no space in between any longer. And that is what makes the Purple Paradigm slightly wonky now... Because if Practice and Instruments can equate to thoughts and intentions and gestures, then the Purple Paradigm is saying that even THOSE are being given up. So not only does magic become flavorless pap where something just happens (something indescribable for vulgar or something that could make sense if not), but it's actually going to happen in an indescribably way. With no thought or intention or action.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I understand your thought pattern.<br /> <br /> Like always the rules leave many things in limbo.<br /> <br /> You could certainly formulate instruments in a way, that they pose no hindrance in play.<br /> <br /> Or you can at first formulate your instruments as a pain in the *** (low Arete), and gradually begin to change your instruments to a state where the difference to \u201cno instrument needed\u201c is blurred.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-10T09:46:19-07:00","id":1102285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1100543-dropping-instruments-wise-what-constitutes-a-technomancer?p=1102168#post1102168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually, with the advent of Focus, THEY ARE. If Instruments just included magic words, circle, gadgets, whatever, you might might be right, but with ideas and thoughts being Instruments and Instruments existing within the framework of Practice.... It's not a vague-ish &quot;thing&quot; out there like pre-M20 paradigm was. If Tools = Instruments then they do link so tight into paradigm/practice that there is no space in between any longer. And that is what makes the Purple Paradigm slightly wonky now... Because if Practice and Instruments can equate to thoughts and intentions and gestures, then the Purple Paradigm is saying that even THOSE are being given up. So not only does magic become flavorless pap where something just happens (something indescribable for vulgar or something that could make sense if not), but it's actually going to happen in an indescribable way. With no thought or intention or action.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those thoughts are still instruments though, and subject to things like time restrictions and skill checks. The psychic needs to concentrate or meditate, the mathemagician needs to calculate his key equations, the postulant needs to formulate his plea. These are the things that are dropped, not the psychic understanding, mathemagic, or faith.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":758,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","user":"Ramnesis","date":". 06-10-2017, 03:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-11T09:26:40-07:00","id":1102531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1100543-dropping-instruments-wise-what-constitutes-a-technomancer?p=1102285#post1102285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Those thoughts are still instruments though, and subject to things like time restrictions and skill checks. The psychic needs to concentrate or meditate, the mathemagician needs to calculate his key equations, the postulant needs to formulate his plea. These are the things that are dropped, not the psychic understanding, mathemagic, or faith.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure I buy that. A thought form doesn't need to be meditated on. Otherwise it would require that it be adjunct to meditation. Bring the form to mind and BOOM. It's like a mental mudra. <br /> <br /> But, even better, how about mathematics and equations? You don't HAVE to make Ability rolls to use your Instruments, either. Never says that. Anymore than you have to use up your Resources or make a Finance roll if you have Money as an Instrument. And with the right level of skill (which can be Merits or Abilitiy dots or whatever), characters can instantly solve math problems with a thought. <br /> <br /> I think I am apprehending an interesting additional quandry. If you can surpass all seven Instruments are you still limited by Practice? I bring that up because it seems like it might feed into your responses as a rationale for what you are proposing and against my arguments. Because, if a mage still has to adhere to his Practice, no matter the need for Instruments, there is still something, even if it's approaching the ineffable.<br /> <br /> For example: A Cultist with the Instrument of Drugs &amp; Poisons and some related Practice (Shamanism? Crazy Wisdom? Medicine-Work?... Yoga?, probably some synthesis...) wouldn't NEED to take his drugs and get high anymore to achieve a desired effect, but if he still had to adhere to the baseline Practice, whatever it is, even if he's not using. I guess, he would have to re-experience or re-create the high (ennact the Practice) without the drug (the surpassed Instrument).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-12T05:45:04-07:00","id":1102779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1100543-dropping-instruments-wise-what-constitutes-a-technomancer?p=1102531#post1102531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not sure I buy that. A thought form doesn't need to be meditated on. Otherwise it would require that it be adjunct to meditation. Bring the form to mind and BOOM. It's like a mental mudra.<br /> <br /> But, even better, how about mathematics and equations? You don't HAVE to make Ability rolls to use your Instruments, either. Never says that. Anymore than you have to use up your Resources or make a Finance roll if you have Money as an Instrument. And with the right level of skill (which can be Merits or Abilitiy dots or whatever), characters can instantly solve math problems with a thought.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, you don't have to, but if a character is in a situation that it would be really hard to use his instruments you better believe I might call for one anyways.<br /> <br /> I'm also not sure I buy the instantly solve idea. Genius and skill may reduce the time something takes, but I can't see a mathematics based paradigm being simple to calculate in your head. Higher order math isn't that fast, some of those calculations should take hours or days. Even if most of that takes place in the undefined off screen hours, I'd stills say the situational calculations take a significant chunk of time or require an external calculating device.<br /> <br /> Which is not to say that I don't see your point. There's enough pop culture examples of people using psychic abilities and the like in an almost reflexive way. I just find that those examples map better to someone who's dropped a few instruments. Most Practices should have some pretty significant difficulties, if for no other reason than because the Mage has to justify why they work to herself.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think I am apprehending an interesting additional quandry. If you can surpass all seven Instruments are you still limited by Practice? I bring that up because it seems like it might feed into your responses as a rationale for what you are proposing and against my arguments. Because, if a mage still has to adhere to his Practice, no matter the need for Instruments, there is still something, even if it's approaching the ineffable.<br /> <br /> For example: A Cultist with the Instrument of Drugs &amp; Poisons and some related Practice (Shamanism? Crazy Wisdom? Medicine-Work?... Yoga?, probably some synthesis...) wouldn't NEED to take his drugs and get high anymore to achieve a desired effect, but if he still had to adhere to the baseline Practice, whatever it is, even if he's not using. I guess, he would have to re-experience or re-create the high (ennact the Practice) without the drug (the surpassed Instrument). </div> </div> </div>For the CoX, I figure the paradigm involves getting into the right ecstatic mental state to accomplish whatever your goal is. The more practice and familiarity the mage has with that mental state the more easily they can just drop into it without any effort.<br /> <br /> Given the penalties for a massive change in focus, particularly that she must return to the full seven instruments no matter how many she already dropped, Practice looks like something that exists beyond instruments. That said, once all the instruments are optional the limitations of Practice are more about what the mage would even consider doing and what it looks like. That CoXer isn't going to evaporate someone with a neutron disintigrator, but that doesn't mean she can't make them fall apart into nothingness.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-12T10:01:00-07:00","id":1102841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1100543-dropping-instruments-wise-what-constitutes-a-technomancer?p=1102779#post1102779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That said, once all the instruments are optional the limitations of Practice are more about what the mage would even consider doing and what it looks like. That CoXer isn't going to evaporate someone with a neutron disintigrator, but that doesn't mean she can't make them fall apart into nothingness.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's the thing I think is really salient, but not overt at all. The Arete 9 Celestial Chorister is still going to have to shape the magic somehow. It's not just pure wishcrafting (though, depending on how internalized the Practice could be, it might look like it). She won't be using the Instruments of a different Sect or Practice, but she it won't be that she's doing nothing. E.g. when a mystic mage gets to Arete 9 they are still doing some kind of magic that looks like something that is limited by the way in which they have always perceived it. <br /> <br /> Though, now that I think on it, talking about Arete 9 mage PCs is pretty much like talking about Generation 5-6 Vampire PCs; so ethereal that it's barely germane.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-13T00:08:22-07:00","id":1103031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1100543-dropping-instruments-wise-what-constitutes-a-technomancer?p=1102841#post1102841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's the thing I think is really salient, but not overt at all. The Arete 9 Celestial Chorister is still going to have to shape the magic somehow. It's not just pure wishcrafting (though, depending on how internalized the Practice could be, it might look like it). She won't be using the Instruments of a different Sect or Practice, but she it won't be that she's doing nothing. E.g. when a mystic mage gets to Arete 9 they are still doing some kind of magic that looks like something that is limited by the way in which they have always perceived it. <br /> <br /> Though, now that I think on it, talking about Arete 9 mage PCs is pretty much like talking about Generation 5-6 Vampire PCs; so ethereal that it's barely germane.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed.<br /> But that still leaves situations where the PC has shed enough instruments for the feat at hand to be performed without instruments.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a> has created a HR that lets you skip instruments for all effects with a highest sphere equal to half your Arete or less.<br /> <br /> This gave me the idea for a variation.<br /> It is quite a bit less formalized, more on the hand wavy side.<br /> <br /> I use the chart feats of magick in addition to the highest sphere rank plus I blend in the Focus to judge what effects can be done without instruments.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}